0331 | Theorem \ref{big} answers one of the open problems posed in \cite{f2uf2}, namely we now can say that the minimum distance of a self-dual code over $\FF_2+u\FF_2$ of length $36$ can be at most $12$.
0332 | \end{remark}
0333 | \begin{remark}
0334 | Theorem \ref{big}, combined with \cite{selfdualRk} implies that the $[72,36,16]$-code cannot be the image of a linear code over $R_k$.
0335 | \end{remark}
