0386 |  \begin{thm}
0387 |  There does not exist a linear code over $\FF_2 + v\FF_2$ whose image is a $[72,36,16]$ Type~II code.
0388 |  \end{thm}
0389 |  \begin{proof}
0390 |  If $C$ is a code over $\FF_2 + v\FF_2$ whose image is a $[72,36,16]$ Type~II code, then $C$ must be a  self-dual code.  If $C$ is a self-dual code over $\FF_2+v\FF_2$ then $C=CRT(C_1,C_2)$, where $C_1,C_2$ are binary self-dual codes,  with minimum weight at least 16 and length 36.  However, it is shown in \cite{shadow} there are no length  36 binary self-dual codes with minimum distance 16.  Hence there is no linear code over $\FF_2 + v\FF_2$ whose image is a $[72,36,16]$ Type~II code.
0391 |  \end{proof}
